'''Marta Díaz de Lope Díaz''' (born 14 February 1988) is a Spanish filmmaker. She has directed ''[[Hopelessly Devout]]'' (2018), ''[[Good Manners (2023 film)|Good Manners]]'' (2023), and ''[[Another League]]'' (2026).

== Life and career ==
Marta Díaz de Lope Díaz was born on 14 February 1988 in [[Ronda]].<ref name="cineuropa">{{Cite web|website=[[Cineuropa]]|date=26 April 2022|url=https://cineuropa.org/en/newsdetail/424495/|title=Marta Díaz de Lope Díaz in post-production with Good Manners|first=Alfonso|last=Rivera|access-date=11 October 2026}}</ref> In 2012, she earned a degree from the [[Cinema and Audiovisual School of Catalonia|ESCAC]] film school in Catalonia with a specialisation in directing.<ref name="cineuropa" /> Early body work included her short films ''Y otro año, perdices'' (2013) and ''Los pestiños de mamá'' (2016) as well as the direction of some episodes of the series ''Brigada de fenómenos''.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.diariosur.es/festival-malaga/equilibrio-constante-drama-comedia-marta-diaz-lope-20230312161655-nt.html|website=[[Diario Sur]]|publisher=[[Grupo Vocento]]|date=12 March 2023|first=Alba|last=Tenza|title=Marta Díaz de Lope, una equilibrista entre el drama y la comedia|language=es-ES|access-date=11 October 2026}}</ref>

Her feature film debut, the comedy ''[[Hopelessly Devout]]'' (2018), tackled a story of female empowerment against the backdrop of the [[Semana Santa]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.canalsur.es/rtva/comunicacion/marta-diaz-agradece-canal-sur_1_1039431.html|website=[[Canal Sur]]|date=21 November 2018|title=Marta Díaz agradece a Canal Sur el Premio Mejor Cineasta de Andalucía|language=es-ES|access-date=11 October 2026}}</ref> It was followed by the comedy-drama ''[[Good Manners (2023 film)|Good Manners]]'' (2023) about the broken family relationship of two sisters at odds with each other.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.canalsur.es/noticias/andalucia/cultura/buenos-modales-rondena-marta-diaz_1_1224765.html|date=3 May 2023|title="Los buenos modales", de la rondeña Marta Díaz, llega a los cines|website=[[Canal Sur]]|access-date=11 October 2026|language=es-ES}}</ref> She directed episodes of the [[SkyShowtime]] series ''Las invisibles''.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://cineconn.es/series-espanolas-de-skyshowtime/|website=Cine con Ñ|title=SkyShowtime estrenará en España las nuevas series del creador de ‘Merlí’ y de Félix Sabroso|date=14 March 2023|language=es-ES|access-date=11 October 2026}}</ref> Her third film, ''[[Another League]]'' (2026) was co-written along with Zebina Guerra and dealt with the pioneers of women's football in Spain.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://kinotico.es/actualidad/2026-03-09/marta-diaz-lope-mujeres-inspiran-pioneras-han-dicho-pelicula-llevarian-ver-sus-nietas|website=Kinótico|title=Marta Díaz de Lope: "Las mujeres que inspiran 'Pioneras' nos han dicho que es la película que llevarían a ver a sus nietas"|date=9 March 2026|first=Daniel|last=Mantilla|language=es-ES|access-date=11 October 2026}}</ref>

